      {
        "category": "legal_disclaimer",
        "text": "The Netherlands Cyber Security Center (henceforth: NCSC-NL) maintains this page to enhance access to its information and security advisories. The use of this security advisory is subject to the following terms and conditions:\n\n    NCSC-NL makes every reasonable effort to ensure that the content of this page is kept up to date, and that it is accurate and complete. Nevertheless, NCSC-NL cannot entirely rule out the possibility of errors, and therefore cannot give any warranty in respect of its completeness, accuracy or continuous keeping up-to-date. The information contained in this security advisory is intended solely for the purpose of providing general information to professional users. No rights can be derived from the information provided therein.\n\n    NCSC-NL and the Kingdom of the Netherlands assume no legal liability or responsibility for any damage resulting from either the use or inability of use of this security advisory. This includes damage resulting from the inaccuracy of incompleteness of the information contained in the advisory.\n    This security advisory is subject to Dutch law. All disputes related to or arising from the use of this advisory will be submitted to the competent court in The Hague. This choice of means also applies to the court in summary proceedings."
      },
      {
        "category": "description",
        "text": "Juniper heeft meerdere kwetsbaarheden verholpen in Junos OS. ",
        "title": "Feiten"
      },
      {
        "category": "description",
        "text": "De kwetsbaarheden bevinden zich in verschillende componenten van Junos OS, waaronder de VXLAN Gateway Daemon (vgd), kmd op MX Series routers, SDK service met JDAF routing, TWAMP client (rmopd service), gRPC library, ipfd daemon op SRX Series, dot1x daemon op Fusion Aggregation Devices, routing protocol daemon (rpd) op MX Series, jdhcpd process, authd process, kernel bij Extended Echo, pkid component, UTM Anti-Spam SBL component op SRX Series, J-Web management interface, en srxpfe component op SRX Series met chassis-cluster configuratie.\n\nEen aanvaller kan deze kwetsbaarheden misbruiken door het versturen van speciaal vervaardigde pakketten of berichten, vaak zonder authenticatie, wat kan leiden tot crashes van processen of het gehele systeem, denial of service, of in sommige gevallen uitvoering van arbitraire code met root privileges.\n\nDe kwetsbaarheden zijn specifiek gebonden aan bepaalde functies of configuraties binnen Junos OS, zoals het gebruik van Security Intelligence feeds, dot1x synchronisatie, HFRR link protection, DHCP client operaties, RADIUS authenticatie, Extended Echo feature, CMP enrollment, Anti-Spam SBL inspectie, J-Web interface, en chassis-cluster fabric traffic. Sommige kwetsbaarheden kunnen worden misbruikt door een aanvaller binnen het netwerk of door een gecompromitteerde externe entiteit zoals een SDN-controller of een RADIUS server.",
        "title": "Interpretaties"
      },
      {
        "category": "description",
        "text": "Juniper heeft updates uitgebracht om de kwetsbaarheden in Junos OS te verhelpen. Zie bijgevoegde referenties voor meer informatie.",
        "title": "Oplossingen"
      },
